---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DonateButton from '../components/DonateButton.astro';
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="In Memoriam"
  description="Kidz 4 A Cure was founded in memory of Kimberly Johnson and Ceyra. This page honors their lives, their spirits, and the legacy they left behind."
>

  <!-- Page Hero — Subdued, dignified -->
  <section class="bg-gradient-to-b from-neutral-800 to-neutral-900 py-20 sm:py-28 text-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <Icon name="mdi:candle" class="w-14 h-14 text-brand-gold-light mx-auto mb-6 opacity-90" />
      <h1 class="font-display font-bold text-4xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl leading-tight mb-6">
        In Memoriam
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-white/75 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mx-auto italic">
        "For Those We Love, For Those We've Lost"
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Introduction -->
  <section class="bg-neutral-50 py-16 sm:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <p class="text-neutral-700 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        Kidz 4 A Cure exists because of love. Two young lives — too brief, too bright — inspired a mission that has touched hundreds of children over two decades. This page is dedicated to honoring them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Kimberly Johnson -->
  <section class="bg-white py-16 sm:py-24 border-b border-neutral-100">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center">
        <!-- Photo Placeholder -->
        <div class="flex flex-col items-center">
          <div class="w-56 h-56 rounded-full bg-neutral-200 flex items-center justify-center mb-6 ring-4 ring-brand-gold/20 shadow-lg">
            <Icon name="mdi:account-circle" class="w-40 h-40 text-neutral-400" />
          </div>
          <div class="text-center">
            <div class="inline-block bg-brand-gold-pale text-brand-gold text-xs font-bold px-4 py-1.5 rounded-full uppercase tracking-wider">
              Photo Placeholder
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Content -->
        <div>
          <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-neutral-500 text-sm mb-4">
            <Icon name="mdi:heart" class="w-4 h-4 text-brand-red" />
            <span>The Heart of Our Mission</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-neutral-900 mb-2 leading-tight">
            Kimberly Johnson
          </h2>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm font-medium mb-6 tracking-wide">
            1992 — 2000 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Age 8
          </p>
          <div class="space-y-4 text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed">
            <p>
              Kimberly was adopted by Lorraine Cram — and she was, by every account, a child full of life, laughter, and a spirit too big for her small frame. She loved the holidays. She loved being celebrated.
            </p>
            <p>
              In 2000, Kimberly lost her battle with HIV/AIDS at the age of eight years old. Her passing left a void that no words could fill. But it also left behind something else: a profound question that Lorraine refused to let go unanswered.
            </p>
            <p>
              What if every child like Kimberly — every child navigating illness, hardship, and uncertainty — could feel, at least once a year, exactly how loved and valued they truly are?
            </p>
            <p>
              Kidz 4 A Cure is Lorraine's answer to that question. Kimberly's name, and her memory, travels in every gift given, every wish fulfilled, every child told: <em class="text-neutral-900">"You matter."</em>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Ceyra -->
  <section class="bg-neutral-50 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-12 items-center">
        <!-- Content -->
        <div class="order-2 lg:order-1">
          <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-neutral-500 text-sm mb-4">
            <Icon name="mdi:heart" class="w-4 h-4 text-brand-red" />
            <span>Added to the Team in 2010</span>
          </div>
          <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-neutral-900 mb-2 leading-tight">
            Ceyra
          </h2>
          <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm font-medium mb-6 tracking-wide">
            Passed 2010
          </p>
          <div class="space-y-4 text-neutral-700 leading-relaxed">
            <p>
              Lorraine's second adopted daughter, Ceyra, passed away in 2010. Like Kimberly before her, Ceyra's life was full of love — and far too short.
            </p>
            <p>
              After Ceyra's passing, Lorraine added her name to the Kidz 4 A Cure team shirts. Side by side — Kimberly and Ceyra — their names have been carried on every AIDS Walk, at every Operation: Holiday Cheer, with every gift wrapped and delivered.
            </p>
            <p>
              Their stories are the reason this organization exists. Their spirits are woven into every act of service K4AC performs. Every child who receives a gift in their honor carries a piece of their legacy forward.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Photo Placeholder -->
        <div class="order-1 lg:order-2 flex flex-col items-center">
          <div class="w-56 h-56 rounded-full bg-neutral-200 flex items-center justify-center mb-6 ring-4 ring-brand-gold/20 shadow-lg">
            <Icon name="mdi:account-circle" class="w-40 h-40 text-neutral-400" />
          </div>
          <div class="text-center">
            <div class="inline-block bg-brand-gold-pale text-brand-gold text-xs font-bold px-4 py-1.5 rounded-full uppercase tracking-wider">
              Photo Placeholder
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Quote / Reflection -->
  <section class="bg-neutral-900 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <Icon name="mdi:format-quote-open" class="w-10 h-10 text-brand-gold-light mx-auto mb-6 opacity-60" />
      <blockquote class="font-display font-bold text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-white leading-relaxed mb-8">
        Their names travel with us. Their love is the foundation of everything we build.
      </blockquote>
      <p class="text-neutral-400 leading-relaxed text-lg">
        When a child receives a gift through Operation: Holiday Cheer, they are receiving something that Kimberly and Ceyra's memory made possible. They are part of a legacy of love that grows every single year.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Tribute section -->
  <section class="bg-white py-16 sm:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <div class="w-16 h-16 bg-brand-gold/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-6">
        <Icon name="mdi:flower-outline" class="w-8 h-8 text-brand-gold" />
      </div>
      <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-neutral-900 mb-4">
        Leave a Tribute
      </h2>
      <p class="text-neutral-600 leading-relaxed mb-8">
        Would you like to leave a message in memory of Kimberly or Ceyra, or share a memory of someone you've loved and lost to HIV/AIDS? Reach out to us — we'd be honored to hear your story.
      </p>
      <a
        href="mailto:kidz4acure1993@gmail.com?subject=In Memoriam Tribute"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-neutral-900 text-white font-semibold px-6 py-3 rounded-full hover:bg-neutral-800 transition-colors"
      >
        <Icon name="mdi:email-outline" class="w-4 h-4" />
        Share a Memory
      </a>

      <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-neutral-100">
        <p class="text-neutral-500 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Honor their memory with a gift that changes a child's life.
        </p>
        <DonateButton href="/donate" label="Donate in Their Memory" variant="primary" size="md" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
